# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Concolic run dumps — raw DSE output.
#
# One dump_<label>.json per distinct explored path. A full experiment run is
# ~29,000 files / ~419 MB, dominated by posts/reshares_create (26,102 dumps,
# 398 MB), and they are regenerated wholesale by the batch runners.
#
# What IS tracked is everything derived from them: REPORT.md,
# coverage_summary.json, exploration_summary.json, seed_index.json and the
# batch-level index files. Those are the analysis products; the dumps are the
# raw material. Reproduce with the per-batch runner named in each REPORT.md.
#
# SCOPED to diaspora/results on purpose. The dumps under
# trivial-concolic-demo/ and chattermate-get-chat-detail/ are 11 small files
# (76 KB) that CONCOLIC_INSTRUCTIONS.md points new agents at as the worked
# reference examples — they stay tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
diaspora/results/**/dump_*.json
# results2/results3 run dumps — same convention: raw DSE output, regenerated
# by the per-endpoint runners (run_dse.rb). Analysis products (coverage_*.json,
# *_summary.json, REPORT.md, targets.rb, run_dse.rb) remain tracked.
diaspora/results2/**/dump_*.json
diaspora/results3/**/dump_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# results3 analysis products that outgrew GitHub.
#
# The policy above — "the dumps are the raw material, everything derived from
# them is tracked" — stops holding for three results3 endpoints. Their
# coverage summaries and assumption/demand files grew with the exploration:
# notifications_index/coverage_summary.json is now 164 MB and
# _assumptions_declared.json 119 MB, both past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so
# a push carrying them is rejected outright. conversations_index (18 MB + 15 MB)
# and comments_index (8 MB + 6.6 MB + 6.3 MB) are under the limit but well past
# the 50 MB warning, and they grow every cycle.
#
# These are derived, not primary: each one is regenerated by its endpoint's
# runner (results3/<endpoint>/run_dse.rb, then the checker pass) from the dumps
# and targets.rb, which stay reproducible. REPORT.md keeps the numbers a reader
# actually needs, and it stays tracked.
#
# SCOPED to the three affected endpoint directories on purpose, and to the
# exact filenames that blew up. The other 130 tracked coverage_summary.json
# files — 119 under diaspora/results, 7 under diaspora/results2, the small
# results3 ones (people_show, _experiment/variant_a), and the two worked
# reference examples under chattermate-get-chat-detail/ and
# trivial-concolic-demo/ — are all well under 1 MB and stay tracked. A blanket
# **/coverage_summary.json would untrack all 133 to solve a 3-file problem.
# Likewise _demand_suffixes.json (542 B) is left out of the _demand_*_* glob.
#
# Already-committed copies are smaller than the current ones (81 MB across the
# 16 at 47cf416), so they remain in history; untracking stops the growth, it
# does not shrink the clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
diaspora/results3/notifications_index/coverage_summary.json
diaspora/results3/notifications_index/_assumptions_declared.json
diaspora/results3/notifications_index/_demand_*_*.json
diaspora/results3/notifications_index/_demandR_*.json
diaspora/results3/conversations_index/coverage_summary.json
diaspora/results3/conversations_index/_assumptions_declared.json
diaspora/results3/comments_index/coverage_summary.json
diaspora/results3/comments_index/_assumptions_declared.json
diaspora/results3/comments_index/_assumption_results.json
